{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/529531-interest-check-vampire-the-requiem-1st-edition-play-by-post","id":529531,"title":"[Interest Check] Vampire: The Requiem 1st Edition Play By Post","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-26T19:19:41-07:00","id":529531,"title":"[Interest Check] Vampire: The Requiem 1st Edition Play By Post","content":"I really want to run a game of old-school Vampire: The Requiem using nothing more than the Mortals and Vampire corebooks from 2004, especially as I read more early NWOD books and grow intrigued with them.<br /> <br /> However, do keep in mind that if I do run a Requiem game, there will be two major changes to the game.<br /> <br /> First off, the Strix don't exist in my games at all. Period. Clan Julii was just Clan Ventrue under a different name at the time. The God-Machine also does not exist.<br /> <br /> Second, vampires in my game are not emotionally dead. They are still capable of having a full range of emotions.<br /> <br /> As for the plot and setting, I want to do a wide-open sandbox approach to the game and probably will set it in either Tokyo or Los Angeles. However, I am also considering creating my own fictional American city.<br /> <br /> I intend to include Changeling: The Lost as well, but at a later time when more players join my game once it is up and running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T20:30:50-07:00","id":529560,"title":"","content":"Maybe. Need to hear more first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:23:09-07:00","id":529809,"title":"","content":"I'm interested, although I'd like to hear more details about the game to decide if it's my cup of tea..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6166-maxriderules","name":"Maxriderules","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}